; Sprites: poles (unused)
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $B100+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. No entity definition has page $B1 as its sprite page and no code loads
; $B1 into a register (checked with the definitions and a search of the code), so this page is not displayed with the
; inputs and rooms examined. Frames 0-3 look like a vertical pole above a base of dots; frames 4-7 look like a tall pole
; with different tops (hook, round head, flag, diamond).
@label=SpritesPolesUnused
b$B100 DEFB $16,$00 ; frame 0: pole above dotted base, frame 0
 $B102 DEFB $16,$00
 $B104 DEFB $16,$00
 $B106 DEFB $16,$00
 $B108 DEFB $16,$00
